The future-state architecture establishes a standardized and automated process for building, validating, publishing, and deploying Golden Amazon Machine Images (AMIs) for EC2 workloads.

The objective is to eliminate manual image creation and configuration drift by establishing a repeatable image lifecycle:

Base OS → Hardening → Security Agents → Monitoring → Application Configuration → Testing → Golden AMI Publication → Production Deployment

The architecture should support both Windows and Linux EC2 workloads while allowing operating-system-specific configurations where required.

