5.8 Layer 6 – Golden AMI Publication

After the image passes all validation checks, it becomes an approved Golden AMI.

Each image should have a unique version.

Example Naming Standard
<ORG>-<OS>-<CIS>-<YYYY.MM>-<BUILD>

VDOT-WIN2022-CIS-L1-2026.09.001

VDOT-RHEL9-CIS-L1-2026.09.001
AMI Metadata

The AMI should contain metadata such as:

Attribute	Example
OS	Windows Server 2022
OS Version	21H2
CIS Level	Level 1
Patch Month	September 2026
Image Version	2026.09.001
Build Date	25-Sep-2026
Source AMI	<AMI-ID>
Security Scan	Passed
Vulnerability Scan	Passed
Approval Status	Approved
Publication

The approved AMI can then be:

Published to approved AWS accounts.
Shared with approved environments.
Registered in an AMI catalog.
Referenced through AWS Systems Manager Parameter Store.
Consumed by Terraform.
