5.15 Golden AMI Lifecycle

The AMI lifecycle should be version-controlled.

AMI v1
  |
  | New security patches
  | New CIS baseline
  | New agent version
  | New OS updates
  ▼
AMI v2
  |
  ▼
Testing
  |
  ▼
Approval
  |
  ▼
Production
  |
  ▼
AMI v3

Older AMIs should be retired according to an approved retention policy.

The retirement process should include:

Identify AMIs no longer used.
Confirm no production resources depend on them.
Mark them deprecated.
Retain the required rollback versions.
Deregister obsolete AMIs.
Remove associated snapshots according to retention policy.
